{"case_id":"T8055","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","attack_surface"],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["encode_row"],"reason":"H0 exclusively exercises PNG decoding through spng_decoded_image_size(), spng_decode_image(), and spng_decode_row(); it never invokes an encoding entry point capable of reaching encode_row(). This leaves the encoder attack surface uncovered in both S0 and S1. The commit only changes the internal memset() bound inside the already-existing encode_row() from len to ctx->subimage[pass].scanline_width; it adds no entry point, protocol, state, configuration, or input semantics and therefore does not introduce or materially aggravate the historical harness gap.","evidence":["H0 creates a context with spng_ctx_new() and supplies encoded PNG input through spng_set_png_file(), spng_set_png_stream(), or spng_set_png_buffer().","H0 calls decoding APIs spng_decoded_image_size(), spng_decode_image(), and spng_decode_row(), but no encoding API.","The sole production change is within static int encode_row(spng_ctx *ctx, const void *row, size_t len).","The changed statement replaces memset(scanline, 0, len) with memset(scanline, 0, ctx->subimage[pass].scanline_width), without altering the function's reachability or public interface."],"recommended_action":"No maintenance is required for this commit. An encoder-specific harness could be added separately to address the pre-existing coverage gap around encode_row()."}
